# Creating agent rules (Cursor + Claude)

Prefer **one source of truth**. Do not paste the same tables/prose into both `claude.md` and `.cursor/rules/`.

## Where content lives

| Guidance | Put it in |
| --- | --- |
| Cross-cutting must-dos every agent needs (short) | `claude.md` |
| Narrow / file-specific / long examples or mapping tables | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` with `globs` (and `alwaysApply: false` unless truly global) |
| Already documented in `claude.md` | Thin Cursor rule that **points** at that section — do not copy it |

`claude.md` is the **index**, not the encyclopedia. It is always loaded into agent context — every extra section costs tokens on every turn.

## Size heuristics

- Prefer Cursor rules **under ~50 lines**, one concern each.
- If a new chunk is **>~40 lines** or only applies to some files, do **not** dump it into `claude.md` — add/extend a `.mdc` rule (or a small doc) and leave a **5-line summary + pointer** in `claude.md` only when Claude Code must see it.
- Before adding to `claude.md`, check whether an existing section or `.cursor/rules/` file already covers it.

## Cursor rule format

`.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` with YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
description: Short rule picker blurb
globs: "**/optional/path/**/*.{tsx,scss}"  # omit or leave broad only if needed
alwaysApply: false  # true only for truly global nudges
---
```

Actionable checklist + bad/good examples. No duplicate of `claude.md`.

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] Single source of truth (no duplicated mapping tables)
- [ ] `claude.md` stayed short or only gained a pointer/summary
- [ ] Narrow rules use `globs`; `alwaysApply: true` is justified
